The home xml nodes have package attr "com.towneers.www" but node() in listXml doesn't include package. We can detect "당근 홈" vs app by presence of `package="com.towneers.www"`? Hmm homeXml has package attr. But the fallback detection need not rely on package: if after one back we're not on sales and no 그만두기, just reopen sales via openSales. That's robust: pressing back once from an in-app sheet returns to list usually; if it went home, deep link reopens sales. If the first back didn't leave a modal (e.g. nested), openSales' deep-link am start also resolves it. So simplify backToSales: try up to 4 iterations: dump; if onSales return; if 그만두기 tap and continue; else press back once; if next dump onSales return; else break and openSales. Actually openSales itself dumps and starts intent. But openSales doesn't press back. Let's restructure:

```
function backToSales(serial, exec, ops) {
  for (let i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
    const xml = dumpXml(serial, exec);
    if (salesReady(xml)) return;
    const discard = ...
    if (discard) { tap 그만두기; continue; }
    if (i > 0) break;
    back once
  }
  openSales(serial, exec);  // if still not sales, deep link
}
```
Hmm but openSales re-dumps. Fine.

Wait: test 2 expects no stray swipes and no leftApp; also expects `tapped` all 3. With landHome: after back from tip → mode: if landHome and mode is not home/kakao → home, else kakao. When back is pressed from tip, mode="tip" → "home" (since mode not home/kakao) top=0. Then our code dumps home xml: not onSales; no 그만두기; break loop; openSales → dumps home (not onSales) → am start karrot://my_sales → mode list, top 0. Then loop? openSales ends. Good, one back total, stray swipes 0, leftApp false.

But in the landHome fake, back from "home" → kakao marking leftApp. So ensure only one back when not sales. In loop above: i=0 back; then i=1 dump: not sales, no discard, i>0 → break. Then openSales. Good.

But what about a case where two backs are needed legitimately and landHome false? E.g. price edit form → back → maybe an intermediate screen? The test at line 200 (`if KEYCODE_BACK screen = list`) is single-level. Existing 4-iteration loop suggests need. But after back, if screen becomes list → onSales. If it became some non-sales screen in app (not home), our new code would deep link sales — also fine and safe. So minimizing backs to at most 1 unless 그만두기 appears seems reasonable. Hmm, but there's risk in real usage: back from keyboard? The KEYCODE_BACK also used by confirmMatchingPrice. Fine.

Actually safer: keep pressing back while the current screen is a known in-app sheet. But we can't identify reliably. The comment in test 2 says exactly: "창을 닫은 뒤 당근 홈으로 떨어지면 back 으로 앱을 나가지 않고 판매관리를 다시 연다" → intended fix: after back, if not sales, reopen sales instead of back again.

So implement: after one back, check sales; if not, openSales (deep link). But what if the sheet needs more backs (e.g., discard dialog)? That's handled by 그만두기 tap before back. I'll allow up to 2 backs only if the second screen still contains known sheet markers? Simpler: at most 1 back, then openSales.

Wait one more consideration: the fake for line 200 test: back from tip → list; onSales yes. OK.

